data.comment:
Intake questions for producer review — the brief is drafted in the description (headline, user stories, 7 acceptance criteria, constraints, key files, risks). Three blocking questions and one non-blocking question need answers before implementation can proceed.

**Q1 (blocking) — Health model.** A five-hit regular enemy contradicts the GDD's explicit "all regular enemies (E1–E5) are 1 HP" and "no multi-hit bullet" rules, and the current 1-HP collision path. Options:
(a) generalise health data-driven (new `health` CSV column + config type/codec + GDD update; P4 Bomb still deals no damage);
(b) keep a Harvester-only code constant;
(c) something else.
**Recommended:** (a) — smallest durable change, serves future multi-hit enemies, keeps tuning in the CSV. Sub-question: should each non-lethal hit show a health indicator (colour/scale), or is ordinary hit feedback enough?

**Q2 (blocking) — Mineral-seeking semantics.** Options:
(a) always seek the nearest live mineral anywhere on the field; absorb on overlap; no firing; cannot steal from the player's hold; re-drop 25–50% per the existing rule;
(b) only seek minerals within a detection radius;
(c) also fire at the player.
**Recommended:** (a) — matches "moves towards the nearest mineral" literally and reuses the whole existing mineral layer.

**Q3 (blocking) — Spawn / campaign integration.** Options:
(a) available in the gym **and** added to the campaign as a rare roaming spawn in later levels;
(b) gym-only archetype for now;
(c) a fixed formation group.
**Recommended:** (a) — playable in the campaign and tuneable in the gym.

**Q4 (non-blocking) — Score and difficulty weight.**
**Recommended:** score ≈ 400 (durable, between Tank 300 and Boss phases); add a `health` factor to `enemyDifficulty` via a separate follow-up item rather than expanding this one.

Also noted: the shared multi-hit seam (`onPlayerBulletHitsEnemy` → `takeDamage`) currently does not finalise a kill (`onEnemyDestroyed`, destruction audio, score, mineral drop). That gap will be closed as part of this work and must be pinned by a test.

Full brief (with generated intake report) remains in the work-item description. Re-run `/skill:intake AH-0MUI820PM0038HS2` once answers are recorded to finish the intake and advance the stage to `intake_complete`.
